;\n- how the six missing F03.7 hazard classes reach it.\n\nCite 08 §4, F03.7 and the Milan and IEEE 1722.1 AECP response-time clauses. Post the design summary as a STOP for a manager ruling if it needs a top-level port, a parameter or a parent-visible change. Otherwise proceed.\n\n**Items, in order:**\n1. **#81 (GAP-07):** the 08 §4 budgets realized: the transaction deadline is read, and the scoreboard kill face is connected.\n2. **#57 (REQ-MVU-005):** T-AECP-RESP. The deadline-kill seam is exercised, and a suite measures MVU response latency against its budget.\n3. **#84 (GAP-10):** all nine F03.7 classes reach the scoreboard, each with a failing arm.\n\nEach item has mutants on the named check, and the resource cost is reported (LUT and FF, out of context).\n\n4. **The parent-visible list.**\n\n**Gates:** as for every PP lane, with the parent consumer set at milan-fpga dev `ccdd07b5` and the combined parent adaptation applied.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/5915626788/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/5915631591","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/81#issuecomment-5915631591","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/81","id":5915631591,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABYJlf5w","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"http