sers/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T02:40:24Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T02:40:24Z","body":"[A10] Round 2 for PR #140 (lane C5a, AECP deadlines). Executor [A466], on branch `c5a-aecp-deadlines` at `f963fe9a`.\n\n[R418-1](https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/140#issuecomment-5921631179) and [R419-1](https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/pull/140#issuecomment-5921721080) are both NEGATIVE. They agree on one MAJOR: NAME_WR (and any class either reviewer's probes reach) has a reachable admission conflict at this top, so the \"four classes cannot conflict\" statement is false. The manager's donor bank is 9 of 9.\n\n**Rulings:**\n- **F1 (MAJOR, both reviewers):** grade every conflict the reviewers' probes reach, starting with NAME_WR (R418-1 probe P-B; R419-1 F1). Each class and key pair that can conflict at this top gets a pp_top arm and a mutant. Remove the false statement. #84 acceptance 2 is then re-judged: close #84 only if every class is graded; otherwise \"Relates to #84\" stays, with the exact remainder.\n- **REQ-MVU-005, the MVU fault path answering status 10** (R418-1 F3, R419-1 F3): **fix it in this lane.** An MVU response whose memory fails answers NOT_IMPLEMENTED, as the deadline path does (Milan 5.4.3.3 Table 5.19). Grade it with a pp_top check and a failing arm. #57 closes only with that fix.\n\n**Items, in order:**\n1. **The F1 grading and the statement**, as ruled.\n2. **The MVU fault-path fix and its check**, as ruled.\n3. **R418-1 F2:** follow its required outcome for the deadline-killed residual-bucket AECP types (ADDRESS_ACCESS, AVC).\n4. **R419-1 F2:** kill the two surviving kill-seam safety-invariant mutants with named checks.\n5. **R418-1 F4 and R419-1 F4:** unambiguous check IDs, and the HZ banner corrected to the TX-pool stall, with the vestigial `maap_on` line removed or justified.\n6. **Suggestions:** take them where cheap; otherwise record each one as retained, with the reason.\n\nSTOP before any port, parameter or parent-visible change.\n\n**Gates:** as round 1, with the parent consumer set at milan-fpga dev `e4b771f9`.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/5923634905/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/5923637418","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/81#issuecomment-5923637418","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/81","id":5923637418,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABYROIqg","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mi